= Content moderation — Technical =

Moderation systems can be modeled as pipelines involving policy definition, detection or reporting, triage, decision, enforcement, notification, appeal, and audit. Automated classifiers introduce measurement error and distribution-shift concerns; human review introduces scale, consistency, and labor constraints.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* content moderation ≠ fact-checking necessarily
* moderation action ≠ proof of falsity
* content moderation ≠ one enforcement action only

